course: dictionary
lesson: 6350
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so you must use the context to find the right one. The word movement is a good example. «Long classical pieces have several parts called movements.» Here a movement is one main part of a long piece of music. The clues are pieces and parts.
explain: «This daily migration is the biggest movement of animals on Earth.» Here movement means moving from place to place. The clue is the animals swimming up and back down each day. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence best?
explain: Movement can also mean a group of people working together to change something, like the environmental movement. Test each meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Movement means changing position or place; moving.
fact: A movement can also be one action of moving, a group working together for change, or one main part of a long piece of music.
fact: Muscles pull on bones at joints to make movement, and all living things move in some way.
fact: «British Sign Language uses hand shapes, movements, the face and the body.»
fact: Plants show movement too, turning towards the light.
exercise: «Long classical pieces have several parts called movements.» In this sentence, what is a movement? | *One main part of a long piece of music | A kind of clapping | A tiny step on the dance floor | A group of musicians on stage
exercise: What does movement mean in the environmental movement? | One action of a hand | *A group of people working together to change something | One main part of a song | Changing place on a map
exercise: «Still pictures shown quickly look like movement.» What does movement mean here? | A sudden scare | *Changing position, so the pictures seem to move | One main part of a piece of music | A group of people working together
test: «Huge numbers of animals swim up from the deep at night... this daily migration is the biggest movement of animals on Earth.» What does movement mean in this sentence? | A group of people protesting | Keeping still in one place | *Moving from place to place | One main part of a piece of music
test: Why should you keep still if an animal is near? | Animals run faster when they are still | *Sudden movements can scare it | Sudden movements make the animal take a nap | Animals like to be stroked when they move
exam: Jayden asks, «What does movement mean in freedom of movement?» | *Freedom to move from place to place | One part of a long song | Freedom to dance at a disco | A group of people protesting
